Test-only: isprime() proof of 1024-bit primes overflows the default 4 MB PARI stack.

diff -urN a/t/genprime_elgamal.t b/t/genprime_elgamal.t
--- a/t/genprime_elgamal.t	2025-01-25 14:13:42.000000000 +0100
+++ b/t/genprime_elgamal.t	2026-11-21 00:03:04.873109484 +0100
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@
 
 use Crypt::Primes; 
 use Math::Pari qw(floor);
+# isprime() proof of a 1024-bit prime needs more than the default 4 MB PARI stack
+Math::Pari::allocatemem(64_000_000);
 
 print "1..10\n";
 
diff -urN a/t/genprime.t b/t/genprime.t
--- a/t/genprime.t	2025-01-25 14:13:42.000000000 +0100
+++ b/t/genprime.t	2026-11-21 00:03:04.872662834 +0100
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@
 
 use Crypt::Primes qw(maurer); 
 use Math::Pari qw(floor);
+# isprime() proof of a 1024-bit prime needs more than the default 4 MB PARI stack
+Math::Pari::allocatemem(64_000_000);
 
 print "1..10\n";
 
